<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibn Rusta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century</span> · Also known as Ahmad ibn Rusta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibn Rusta was a Persian geographer of the early 10th century, probably from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a>, author of the Book of Precious Records. His work includes some of the earliest descriptions of the peoples of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, among them the Rus', the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazars</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyars</a> and the mountain kingdom of Sarir.</p></div>
